WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:10.110
A Republican wonders whether colored people,
his word colored people, get coronavirus more

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:14.700
because they don't know or refuse to wash
their hands.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:19.630
In other words, are dirty immigrants more
likely to get corona virus and they happen

00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:21.330
to be the colored ones?

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:25.359
This is the question from a guy who should
never show his face in public again.

00:00:25.359 --> 00:00:26.739
His name is Steve Huffman.

00:00:26.739 --> 00:00:28.999
He's a Republican state senator in Ohio.

00:00:28.999 --> 00:00:31.289
Didn't really have to tell you he was a Republican.

00:00:31.289 --> 00:00:36.870
As some of you know, Corona virus is disproportionately
hitting the nonwhite population of the United

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:37.870
States.

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:43.699
There are different reasons why some of our
nonwhite populations in the U.S. have more

00:00:43.699 --> 00:00:47.359
underlying health conditions that can be linked
to poverty.

00:00:47.359 --> 00:00:49.940
Often, poverty brings with it poor health.

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:55.719
Preexisting conditions appear to predispose
people to more serious cases of coronavirus.

00:00:55.719 --> 00:01:01.629
You then also have to account for sometimes
having in access to inferior medical services.

00:01:01.629 --> 00:01:03.050
There's a lot of different factors here.

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:08.840
But the point is we know that minorities,
including black Americans, are being disproportionately

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:13.549
hit by corona virus during a hearing about
racism.

00:01:13.549 --> 00:01:21.520
Ohio State Senator Steve Huffman asked, Is
it possible that the black and colored population.

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:27.360
Might be getting hit harder by Corona virus
because they don't wash their hands as well

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:34.431
as white people, essentially, so proposing
the idea that these folks are dirtier, they're

00:01:34.431 --> 00:01:37.680
not washing their hands as well or as frequently.

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:39.539
Now, get ready for this.

00:01:39.539 --> 00:01:40.829
Huffman is a doctor.

00:01:40.829 --> 00:01:46.560
He said, quote, My point is, I understand
African-Americans have a higher incidence

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:50.810
of chronic conditions and it makes them more
susceptible to death from Cauvin.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:51.810
But why?

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:54.490
It doesn't make them more susceptible to just
get kov.

00:01:54.490 --> 00:02:00.200
It could it just be that African-Americans
or the colored population do not wash their

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:05.520
hands as well as other groups or wear a mask
or do not socially distance themselves?

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:08.460
That could be the explanation of the higher
incidence.

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:10.770
Now cut.

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:16.330
Ohio Commissioner, on my note at the Ohio
Commission on Minority Health's director Angela

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:22.800
Dawson said what Huffman is asserting is not
the opinion of leading medical experts in

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:24.500
this country.

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:27.360
That probably doesn't come as a surprise to
you.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:31.291
So either the implication is black people
don't wash their hands correctly because they

00:02:31.291 --> 00:02:35.790
don't know how or black people don't wash
their hands correctly because they're dirty

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:37.690
and they don't care to wash their hands.

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:41.050
Pick your explanation as to what Steve Huffman
is saying here.

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:43.810
And then, of course, you know this reference
to the colored population.

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:45.760
Like, what year are we in again?

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:50.330
And for me, this is more proof that we need
more people from younger generations who it

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:54.930
would never even occur to to use this language
in these positions of power.

00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:58.460
And it's also a reminder that just because
you're a doctor doesn't mean you're necessarily

00:02:58.460 --> 00:02:59.460
smart.

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:02.210
Look at some of the things Ben Carson believes
if you need proof of that.

00:03:02.210 --> 00:03:04.170
Now, one last thing.

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:12.320
Let's for a second take seriously the question
of are there handwashing differences among

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:14.110
populations?

00:03:14.110 --> 00:03:15.120
Because this has been studied.

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:17.350
We're linking to one such study.

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:24.860
And the conclusions from this study were that
women tend to wash their hands more and better.

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:30.930
In other words, using soap and scrubbing long
enough, women are better hand washers than

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:36.290
men, and nonwhite people are better hand washers
than white people.

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:41.900
When this has been studied disproportionately,
white men are the worst offenders when it

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:43.850
comes to bathroom handwashing.

00:03:43.850 --> 00:03:48.650
We're linking to this study in the description
to the YouTube video for this story.

00:03:48.650 --> 00:03:50.320
Certainly something to think about.

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:52.210
This guy should never show his face in public
again

